WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.730
Sagittarius A star.

00:02.458 --> 00:04.528
Nobody can see this black hole itself.

00:04.920 --> 00:12.239
Astronomers watched a star go round it every sixteen years, at millions of kilometres an hour, and worked out what it circles.

00:12.720 --> 00:20.030
Eight radio observatories, working as one telescope the size of the Earth, then photographed glowing gas and a shadow.

00:20.734 --> 00:23.297
Here it is drawn as a model, from its mass.
